<<~ ahu slot=`#/body`>>

''YES.'' A sovereign vessel with an owed seat raise can issue `seat-duties` before the host working layer is mounted.

* ''MEASURED'' — `openNodeVessel` prepares, then composes the vessel. The daemon cap opens the daemon, wires verbs and calls `afterDaemon`; that hook registers `workerEa.then(() => seatSettler.onFold())`. The wiki and primary mount gates also await `workerEa`, and composition finishes before `openNodeVessel` returns. The caller mounts the host layer only afterward. ([[open-node-vessel.ts:3830|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts:3830]], [[core-caps.ts:120|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-tw5/src/core-caps.ts:120]], [[core-caps.ts:158|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-tw5/src/core-caps.ts:158]], [[core-caps.ts:203|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-tw5/src/core-caps.ts:203]], [[main.ts:716|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-node/src/main.ts:716]], [[main.ts:784|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-node/src/main.ts:784]])

* ''MEASURED'' — An owed, unshadowed raise causes the settler to read facts and issue the ask; board changes also trigger refolds and settling, and daemon restart registers another `workerEa` callback. There is no ask timer; two subsequent folds abandon a waiting settle, as do teardown or restart. ([[seat-settle.ts:85|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-node/src/seat-settle.ts:85]], [[edge-shadow-ring.ts:123|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-node/src/edge-shadow-ring.ts:123]], [[open-node-vessel.ts:3122|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts:3122]])

* ''INFER'' — If the outcome arrives before the host layer is attached, the ask can remain pending even after attachment: it checks once, then rechecks on matching change events, while adding a layer forwards future events rather than replaying existing outcomes. The daemon composite initially has no default writable; the separately mounted wiki uses the assembly composite. ([[island-verb-ask.ts:87|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-node/src/island-verb-ask.ts:87]], [[composite-store.ts:139|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-mesh/src/composite-store.ts:139]], [[daemon-vm-core.ts:388|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-tw5/src/daemon-vm-core.ts:388]], [[core-caps.ts:165|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-tw5/src/core-caps.ts:165]])

* ''MEASURED'' — Pool worker events enter a 20 Hz event bus and may place daemon verbs before return; store doors can issue `seat-duties`, `kahua-cap`, and `realm-feed`, while backup doors issue memory asks. The residency sweeper and boot watchdog run timers; the watchdog bounds `workerEa`, not these outcome waits. Main attaches the UDS channel only after mounting. ([[open-node-vessel.ts:3833|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts:3833]], [[open-node-vessel.ts:4042|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts:4042]], [[store-door-verbs.ts:344|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-node/src/store-door-verbs.ts:344]], [[main.ts:791|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-node/src/main.ts:791]])

''MEASURED'' — The repository’s only production call to `openNodeVessel` is `main.ts`; herm uses a separate factory and also mounts before attaching its channel. Neither ordering prevents the internal callback above. ([[main.ts:656|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-node/src/main.ts:656]])

''Red:'' Boot a sovereign vessel with an owed raise, hold `mountHostWorkingLayer`, let its boot-triggered `seat-duties` outcome land, then mount. Assert the ask settles or refuses by name, never hangs. ''INFER'' — This exercises the race; it was not run in this read-only seat.

